# encoder: turning the knob shows the value on the DB8E (issue #19).
# Spec: encoder.md "If you have a DB8E display controller ... the value shows up
# in the display whenever you turn the encoder. It then shows the updated value
# of `output` in the display." — so the body is the SCALED output
# (pos * outputscale + outputoffset), not the raw 0..1 position, and `header`
# rides along.
#
# Scale/offset are the ones from patches/lfo-cc-midi.ini, the patch the hardware
# video was shot with (header "CC RATE HZ", values in the hundreds).
#   pos = detents/96 at sensivity 1; smooth = 0 for exact steps.
#   @0  seed pos 0 -> output 100, but nothing has been TURNED: screen stays off.
#   @1  +48 -> pos 0.5 -> output 0.5*2650 + 100 = 1425
#   @2  no turn -> the screen holds the last value (content persists)
#   @3  -24 -> pos 0.25 -> output 0.25*2650 + 100 = 762.5
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[db8e]

[display]
    takeovercontrols = 1

[encoder]
    encoder      = E1.1
    smooth       = 0
    outputscale  = 2650
    outputoffset = 100
    header       = "CC RATE HZ"
    output       = O1
>>>
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 turn E1.1 48
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 1425 tol 1e-3
@1 expectdisplay D1 header "CC RATE HZ"
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 1425 tol 1e-3
@3 turn E1.1 -24
@3 expectdisplay D1 value 762.5 tol 1e-3
